1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,113
Here is EARN on Solana in two minutes.

2
00:00:03,233 --> 00:00:08,386
We will follow the real system, from the browser to liquidity pools.

3
00:00:08,506 --> 00:00:13,650
And separate that architecture from this repository's new example code.

4
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:20,544
The homepage and vault app use React and TypeScript, served through Cloudflare Workers.

5
00:00:20,664 --> 00:00:24,088
The user's wallet approves and signs transactions.

6
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:30,650
The Worker provides the RPC gateway, market statistics, and Keeper status.

7
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:34,077
A deposit starts with USDC.

8
00:00:34,197 --> 00:00:40,071
The app converts it into the selected asset pair and deposits it in one atomic transaction.

9
00:00:40,191 --> 00:00:45,495
The vault program issues shares and manages liquidity through Raydium CLMM.

10
00:00:45,615 --> 00:00:50,650
Redemption burns shares and returns the underlying asset plus USDC.

11
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:55,936
Keeper coordination lives in a separate Durable Object for each network and vault.

12
00:00:56,056 --> 00:01:00,494
Each vault has one daily strategy slot, in the UTC zero cycle.

13
00:01:00,614 --> 00:01:03,490
A signed transaction is journaled and submitted once.

14
00:01:03,610 --> 00:01:06,703
Pending signatures are checked every forty-five seconds.

15
00:01:06,823 --> 00:01:09,933
Failure or expiry waits for the next daily decision.

16
00:01:10,053 --> 00:01:14,650
Fee-only reinvestment requires ten USDC in combined unclaimed fees.

17
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:21,186
RPC traffic uses a primary Helius provider, a standby, and a public endpoint.

18
00:01:21,306 --> 00:01:25,003
Read failover never means replaying a submitted Keeper transaction.

19
00:01:25,123 --> 00:01:27,807
Homepage market caching is only for display.

20
00:01:27,927 --> 00:01:32,650
Accounting and execution use chain state, while idle app pages avoid polling.

21
00:01:33,450 --> 00:01:37,944
Mainnet and Devnet share program logic, with separate identities and execution policies.

22
00:01:38,064 --> 00:01:41,759
Each network currently publishes six live vaults, and the registry can grow.

23
00:01:41,879 --> 00:01:46,206
Management can independently pause deposits, withdrawals, or strategy investment.

24
00:01:46,326 --> 00:01:49,650
Compatible upgrades preserve existing program and account identities.

25
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:52,516
The diagram reflects the deployed system.

26
00:01:52,636 --> 00:01:56,277
This repository's website and Rust counter are fresh starter examples.

27
00:01:56,397 --> 00:01:59,650
Explore the source, tests, and architecture on GitHub.
